              "content": "<p class=\"nurse-note-row\"><span class=\"nurse-note-time\">1100:</span><span class=\"nurse-note-text\">Serology results reviewed with rheumatologist. Antinuclear Antibody (ANA) is positive with high titer (1:640, homogeneous pattern). Anti-double-stranded DNA (anti-dsDNA) is strongly positive (142 IU/mL). Complement levels (C3 and C4) are low, consistent with active immune-complex consumption. Complete blood count shows mild leukopenia (WBC 3.2 &times; 10⁹/L). Urinalysis reveals 1+ proteinuria (0.3 g/L) and 5–10 RBCs/hpf without casts, indicating early lupus nephritis involvement. Nurse prepares to educate client on photosensitivity protection, renal monitoring, and immunosuppressive therapy.</span></p>"
