              "content": "<p class=\"nurse-note-row\"><span class=\"nurse-note-time\">1445 (Hour 6 Post-Injury):</span><span class=\"nurse-note-text\">Resuscitation parameters: Urine output for the past hour was 48 mL (cumulative 6-hour output: 245 mL, avg 41 mL/hr). Blood pressure 108/68 mmHg, HR 102 bpm. Bilateral radial pulses assessed via Doppler ultrasound: strong biphasic acoustic signals present; brisk capillary refill in nailbeds. Upper extremities elevated on pillows to promote venous return. Serum potassium trending down from 5.8 to 5.1 mmol/L; hematocrit stabilized at 48%. Lactate decreased to 2.4 mmol/L. Total LR infused in first 6 hours: 4,800 mL. On schedule to complete first half by Hour 8.</span></p>"
